{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[],"color":"#F5A623","description":"Troy has fallen. Odysseus holds Astyanax, the son of Hector.","name":"The Horse and the Infant"},{"children":[],"color":"#F5A623","description":"Zeus warns that the child will bring ruin if he lives.","name":"Zeus's Ultimatum"},{"children":[],"color":"#F5A623","description":"Odysseus sacrifices the infant. \"Forgive me.\"","name":"The Choice"}],"color":"#F5A623","description":"The reluctant warrior.","name":"Timeline: Odysseus","timeline_id":1,"timeline_index":1},{"children":[{"children":[],"color":"#D0021B","description":"Zagreus rises from the pool of blood in Hades.","name":"Awakening"},{"children":[],"color":"#D0021B","description":"Zagreus sees Hades conspiring with Apollo.","name":"The Court"},{"children":[],"color":"#D0021B","description":"Conflict with Megaera or another Fury while trying to escape.","name":"Battle vs Fury"},{"children":[],"color":"#D0021B","description":"The death of Astyanax and the fall of Troy cause a massive quake in the Underworld.","name":"The Tremor"},{"children":[],"color":"#D0021B","description":"Zagreus uses the distraction to slip through a crack in the Styx.","name":"Escape via Breach"}],"color":"#D0021B","description":"Prince of the Underworld.","name":"Timeline: Zagreus","timeline_id":0,"timeline_index":2},{"children":[{"children":[],"color":"#BD10E0","description":"Circe watches the events in Hades' court from the shadows.","name":"The Observer"},{"children":[],"color":"#BD10E0","description":"She sees the anomaly (Zagreus) escaping and takes notice.","name":"Noticing the Breach"}],"color":"#BD10E0","description":"The Silent Observer.","name":"Timeline: Circe","timeline_id":0,"timeline_index":0}],"color":"#D0021B","description":"\"Just a Man\" - The Fall of Troy and the Descent.","name":"Saga 1: The Troy Saga","timeline_id":0,"timeline_index":3},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[],"color":"#F5A623","description":"Sailing away from Troy, eager to return to Ithaca.","name":"Full Speed Ahead"},{"children":[],"color":"#F5A623","description":"Odysseus intercepts the strange \"man\" (Zagreus) found in the water.","name":"Meeting Zagreus"},{"children":[],"color":"#F5A623","description":"The crew finds the Lotus Eaters. Caution is key.","name":"Lotus Island"},{"children":[],"color":"#F5A623","description":"Trapped by Polyphemus the Cyclops.","name":"The Cave"},{"children":[],"color":"#F5A623","description":"Odysseus devises the \"Nobody\" trick while Zagreus wants to fight.","name":"The Plan"},{"children":[],"color":"#F5A623","description":"Odysseus reveals his name in hubris after blinding the Cyclops.","name":"My Goodbye"}],"color":"#F5A623","description":"Caption of the ship.","name":"Timeline: Odysseus"},{"children":[{"children":[],"color":"#D0021B","description":"Zagreus emerges in the middle of the ocean, disoriented.","name":"The Surface"},{"children":[],"color":"#D0021B","description":"He joins Odysseus's ship, hiding his divinity.","name":"Joining the Crew"},{"children":[],"color":"#D0021B","description":"Zagreus is baffled by mortal needs and the Lotus fruit.","name":"Lotus Confusion"},{"children":[],"color":"#D0021B","description":"Zagreus tries to rush Polyphemus, nearly ruining the plan.","name":"I Kill Gods"},{"children":[],"color":"#D0021B","description":"Forced to follow Odysseus's stealthier approach.","name":"Restrained"}],"color":"#D0021B","description":"Godling out of water.","name":"Timeline: Zagreus"},{"children":[{"children":[],"color":"#BD10E0","description":"Circe tracks the fugitive Godling through her scrying bowl.","name":"Scrying"},{"children":[],"color":"#BD10E0","description":"She realizes their paths are converging towards Aeaea.","name":"Interest Piqued"}],"color":"#BD10E0","description":"Watching from afar.","name":"Timeline: Circe"}],"color":"#4A90E2","description":"\"Survive\" - Open waters and the first monster.","name":"Saga 2: The Cyclops Saga","timeline_id":0,"timeline_index":1},{"children":[],"color":"#808080","description":"Placeholder","name":"Saga 3: The Ocean Saga","timeline_id":0,"timeline_index":2},{"children":[],"color":"#808080","description":"Placeholder","name":"Saga 4: The Circe Saga","timeline_id":0,"timeline_index":3},{"children":[],"color":"#808080","description":"Placeholder","name":"Saga 5: The Underworld Saga","timeline_id":0,"timeline_index":4},{"children":[],"color":"#808080","description":"Placeholder","name":"Saga 6: The Thunder Saga","timeline_id":0,"timeline_index":6},{"children":[],"color":"#808080","description":"Placeholder","name":"Saga 7: The Wisdom Saga","timeline_id":0,"timeline_index":7},{"children":[],"color":"#808080","description":"Placeholder","name":"Saga 8: The Vengeance Saga","timeline_id":0,"timeline_index":8},{"children":[],"color":"#808080","description":"Placeholder","name":"Saga 9: The Ithaca Saga","timeline_id":0,"timeline_index":9}],"color":"#1A1A1A","description":"Integrated timelines for Odysseus, Zagreus, and Circe across the Sagas.","name":"Epic: The Musical (Sagas)","timeline_id":0,"timeline_index":1}